      "writtenOn": "2020-04-07T05:13:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The type enum isn\u0027t a part of the spec, but it is heavily used in the PRL and PE layers in the new stack so I would be surprised if it were re-ordered.  We already assume the enum order somewhat for NUM_SOP_STAR_TYPES which we use to find the boundary of the transmit types in that enum.\n\nEach port or cable will return one DiscoverIdentity ACK and I don\u0027t know of a way for the contents to differ.  We always want to clear data after a disconnect, so we wouldn\u0027t keep past results.  Technically there are SOP\u0027_Debug and SOP\u0027\u0027_Debug types but I don\u0027t anticipate those being used and don\u0027t want to waste static space.\n\nAre there any situations you\u0027re worried we\u0027re missing here?",
      "parentUuid": "ca2e41d9_e5537938",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 369,
        "startChar": 27,
        "endLine": 369,
        "endChar": 50
      },
      "revId": "3e42453c8d53c140c7f0564e775b9f63bf81ca0f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
